(ned -- StartC, the whole C step. Mirrors cal_a_cycle.)
(  1. cal_c_zero -- probe toward centre at A-45 and A+45 about the corrected)
(                   A zero, rotate C, probe the pair again. ABORTS if its own)
(                   delta got worse.)
(  2. cal_probe_center -- re-find the puck. Rotating C SWINGS THE TOOL TIP,)
(                   so the stored centre must be re-measured or the next)
(                   cycle works against a frame that no longer describes)
(                   this tip. This is also what leaves the machine sitting)
(                   on the MOST UP TO DATE zero at the end.)

o<cal_c_cycle> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, StartC: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, StartC: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif
  (NO SEPARATE TEACH BUTTON -- operator 2026-08-03: overload StartC. The)
  (reference lives in the params, so the params decide what a press does:)
  (   no reference  -> position for the jog and hand back)
  (   jog pending   -> capture what was jogged, then measure)
  (   reference set -> just measure)
  (To re-teach, CLEAR C REF then press StartC. One button, and the state)
  (lives in the data rather than in the operator's head.)
  o7 if [#3058 EQ 0 AND #3059 NE 1]
    o<cal_c_ref> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]
    #3071 = 1
    (PRINT, StartC: no C reference yet - positioned at A -45 one inch in front with the puck up. JOG the tip into place, then press StartC again.)
    (DEBUG, StartC: jog the tip into place, then press StartC again)
    o7 return
  o7 endif

  #3071 = 0

  o<cal_c_zero> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]

  (re-find the puck ONLY if C actually moved -- a discarded correction leaves)
  (the geometry untouched, so the stored centre is still the centre)
  o20 if [#3073 EQ 1]
    (PRINT, StartC: C corrected by #3057 deg, dX #3055 -> #3056. Re-finding the puck so the zero matches the new C.)
    o<cal_probe_center> call
  o20 else
    (PRINT, StartC: correction discarded, C unchanged - skipping the puck re-find, the stored centre is still valid.)
  o20 endif

  #3071 = 1
  (PRINT, StartC DONE: dX #3055 -> #3056, C total #3070 deg, new centre #3045 #3046 top #3047)
  (DEBUG, StartC done: dX #3055 to #3056, new centre #3045 #3046 top #3047)

o<cal_c_cycle> endsub

M2 (end program)
